.TH "tum\-ls" "1" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
\f[B]tum\-ls\f[R] \[em] list every utility pane across all sessions
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tum ls\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]tum ls\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
List every managed utility pane across all sessions, queried from
\f[CR]tmux list\-panes \-a\f[R].
The global view: any session can borrow from the shared pool, so this is
where you see where every instance lives and what it is bound to.
.PP
Columns: Utility, Layout, Host (a session:pane id, or \f[CR]hidden\f[R],
\f[CR]host gone\f[R], or \f[CR]pushed\f[R]), Home (the owning pane, or
\f[CR]pool\f[R]), Slot, Geometry, and State (\f[CR]shown\f[R],
\f[CR]hidden\f[R], \f[CR]pushed\f[R], or \f[CR]orphan\f[R]).
.SS OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R] Print a short synopsis (the SYNOPSIS
and EXAMPLES sections of this page) and exit.
For bare \f[B]tum\f[R], list every subcommand.
.SS EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
tum ls                   # every utility pane, everywhere
# bound to  t g l  in the shipped tum\-bindings.conf
.EE
.SS SEE ALSO
\f[B]tum\-check\f[R](1), \f[B]tum\-status\f[R](1), \f[B]tmux\f[R](1)
